@arc home.sam
who: home:sam
name: Sam
pron: they
// Writer 3, from the head writer's model (mum.call) and the approved arc: Sam (they / them), your best friend since
// school. Plainly platonic: old friends, never a partner, no "I miss you" that could read romantic (they say "the
// bench is boring without you", "the quiz team's useless"). Messages get shorter across the distance; one beat where
// you both admit it; then a standing "Sunday story" swap.
//
// HOW THEY TALK: fast and funny at first, all in one breath, old jokes and nicknames for places; then shorter, flatter
//   messages as the gap grows; honest when it matters. Calls you {me}, or "you absolute idiot", fondly.
// NEVER: romantic, jealous or possessive (they're glad you went); guilt-trips; genders you.
// NEW HERE (to approve): you met on the bench by the school gate at seven; the café quiz on Thursdays (your old team,
//   "the Bench"); Sam works at the library, reshelving; the Sunday story.
// RUNNING: the bench; the quiz team losing without you; the library trolley with the wonky wheel; the Sunday story.

== beat 1
tone: light
via: reply
mem: firstcall
flag: home.sam.called
them: You absolute idiot, you actually went! Into space! I said you wouldn't. I owe the whole quiz team a cake.   [laugh]
them: Tell me everything. Is there a window? Is there a bed? Do you float? Tell me you float a little.
them: The Bench lost at quiz on Thursday. Third from last. Without you we knew nothing about anything. We guessed "a goat" twice.
? choice
* No floating. Lots of corridors. A very good chef.   flavour:cheer mem:nofloat
  them: Disappointing. The chef's good, though? Fine. You're allowed to be happy. Just a bit.
* Tell me about home first.   flavour:listen mem:homefirst
  them: Home? Same as when you left. Four days ago. The bench is still there. It's boring without you on it.
* It's big. I'm a bit lost.   flavour:share mem:lost
  them: You were lost in the school car park for two years. You'll be fine in a spaceship. Give it a week.
them: Right. Long message. Sorry. Not sorry. Write back properly. Pages. I want pages.

== beat 2
tone: light
via: reply
when: flag:home.sam.called
mem: library
flag: home.sam.library
them: Busy week. Library's mad. Someone returned a book eleven years late and wanted a medal.   [laugh]
them: The trolley's still got the wonky wheel. I've named it. It doesn't come when it's called.
them: Quiz was fine. We came fourth. Anyway. How's space? Still big?
? choice
* Fourth! That's nearly a medal.   flavour:cheer mem:fourth
  them: That's what I said! Nobody listened. You'd have listened.
* Your message was shorter this time.   flavour:listen mem:shorter
  them: Was it? Busy week. I'll do a long one next time. Promise.
them: Write back. Tell me something weird about the ship. One weird thing.

== beat 3
tone: heartfelt
via: live
when: beat:home.sam.2
mem: bench
flag: home.sam.bench
hint: The relay's clear tonight. Sam's on the line, live.
them: Live! You're actually there. There's a hum on the line. Is that your ship? Hello, ship.
them: I sat on the bench today. By the school gate. Where we met. We were seven and you had a plaster on your knee.
them: It's daft. Everything here feels too small to tell you. Library, quiz, bench. You've got stars. I've got a trolley.   [sigh]
? choice
* Tell me the small things. I want the small things.   flavour:listen mem:smallthings
  them: Really? All right. The café's changed its biscuits. It's a disaster. Everyone's furious.   [laugh]
  + them: Really? Then here's one. The café's changed its biscuits and the whole quiz team has gone on strike. Small enough?
* Stars are mostly just stars. Your trolley's got a name.   flavour:cheer mem:trolley
  them: It does have a name. It's got more personality than most people. Fine. Point taken.
* It's strange for me too, being this far.   flavour:share mem:strange
  them: Is it? Good. I mean, not good. Good that it's not just me.
them: I've got to go. The relay's beeping. Same bench next week. I'll be on it, anyway.

== beat 4
tone: light
via: reply
when: beat:home.sam.3
mem: short
them: Hi. Busy. Quiz Thursday. Lost. Wheel still wonky. You?   [laugh]
them: That's the whole message. I'm sorry. I wrote a long one and deleted it. It sounded like a weather report.
them: Tell me one thing. One. I'll tell you one back. Deal?
? choice
* Deal. Here's one: I learnt to fold a blanket properly.   flavour:share mem:blanket
  them: You? Properly? I'm framing this message. Here's mine: Mrs Abbot from the café says hello. She never says hello.
* Deal. You first.   flavour:listen mem:youfirst
  them: Fine. I found a postcard in a returned book. Someone's holiday, years ago. I've stuck it on the trolley.
them: See? One thing each. That wasn't so hard. Let's do it again.

== beat 5
tone: serious
via: live
when: beat:home.sam.4
mem: drifting
flag: home.sam.admitted
hint: Clear line tonight. Sam's on, and they're quiet.
them: Can I say it? We're getting shorter. The messages. Yours and mine. I've been counting words. That's how bad it is.   [sigh]
them: I know it's the distance. It's nobody's fault. But we've been friends since the bench. I don't want us to fade out.
them: I'm scared we'll end up as two people who used to be friends. Who send a card once a year. I'd hate that.
? choice
* I've noticed too. I didn't know how to say it.   flavour:listen mem:noticed
  them: Oh, thank goodness. I thought it was just me, being dramatic. I am dramatic. But not about this.
* You're my oldest friend. That doesn't stop because I'm far away.   flavour:share mem:oldest
  them: Yeah. Yeah, it doesn't, does it. Since we were seven. That's a long time to just stop.
  + them: Since we were seven. Plasters and the bench and everything. Right. Then we fix it. Friends fix things.
* Let's make a rule. Something we always send.   flavour:practical mem:rule
  them: A rule. Yes. You were always the one with rules. Go on. What rule?
them: Here's an idea. Every Sunday, one story each. Any story. Even a boring one. Especially a boring one. Deal?

== beat 6
tone: resolution
via: live
when: beat:home.sam.5
mem: sunday
flag: home.sam.sundays
keepsake: Sam's first Sunday story, written on the back of a library card
learn: Sam, your oldest friend, felt you drifting apart. Now you swap one story every Sunday, however small.
mail: 2880 | From Sam | In the post bag: an old library card, written on the back in tiny letters. "Sunday story number one. The wonky wheel came off. I carried it home. It's on my windowsill now. Your turn. Sam"
them: It's Sunday! Story time. I've got a good one. The trolley wheel came off, and I carried it home on the bus.   [laugh]
them: It's on my windowsill now. Like a trophy. A small, squeaky trophy. That's my story. That's the whole of it.
them: This is working, isn't it? I look forward to Sundays now. I've written the first one down. On a library card. It's in the post.
? choice
* Best Sunday story yet.   flavour:cheer mem:best
  them: It's the only Sunday story yet. But I'll take it. Best friend, best story.
* Here's mine. I'll tell it slowly.   flavour:share mem:mine
  them: Go on. Slowly. I've got all evening and a kettle.
  + them: Go on. I've got a kettle, a biscuit, and the wheel watching. Slowly. Every bit of it.
them: Same time next Sunday. Every Sunday. Even when there's nothing. Especially then.

// ---- what you can tell them on a call
== send
? flag:intro.soloJob
- I did my first job on my own.   flavour:share
  them: Look at you! A proper job! The Bench is very proud. I've told them.
? came:any
- We had a {trad} on the ship. I went.   flavour:share
  them: A {trad}? In space? Was there a quiz? Tell me there was a quiz.
? friend:any
- I've made a friend. {friend}.   flavour:share
  them: Good. Tell {friend} hello from the Bench. And ask if they know anything about engines.
?
- Tell me one thing from home.   flavour:listen
  them: The café's got the old biscuits back. Peace has returned to the town.
- How did the Bench do at quiz?   flavour:cheer
  them: Don't. Just don't. There was a question about engines. We needed you.

// ---- everyday calls when no beat is due
== chat
them: Hello, you absolute idiot. Nothing happened today. I'm telling you anyway.
? send
them: Right. Off. The trolley needs me.
--
when: flag:home.sam.sundays weekday:sun
them: It's Sunday! You know what that means. You first this time.   [laugh]
? send
them: Brilliant. Same time next week.
--
when: flag:home.sam.library
them: Quick one from the library. I'm hiding in the atlas section. There's a map of the stars. You're not on it. Rude.
? send
them: Shush, someone's coming. Bye!
